# Line endings are LF everywhere — in the index and in the working tree — and
# that must not depend on how each machine happens to have core.autocrlf set.
# This repo currently has core.autocrlf=true set locally, which would rewrite
# every text file to CRLF on the next checkout; `eol=lf` overrides it.
#
# It matters beyond tidiness: .githooks/pre-commit is a POSIX sh script, and a
# shell script with CRLF endings fails to execute. Everything else here (Node,
# Next, TypeScript, VS Code) reads LF without complaint on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Icons generated by npm run icons. Never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
